      "url": "https://www.senate.mn/schedule/hearing_minutes.html?always_show_minutes=Y&hearing_id=17940&ls=93&type=minutes",
      "sha256": "282157457e4a26d6e047319a028e5c1171a17eed1259bbe7663b0e184ea01833",
      "textSha256": "282157457e4a26d6e047319a028e5c1171a17eed1259bbe7663b0e184ea01833",
      "date": "2023-04-03",
      "committee": "State and Local Government and Veterans",
      "session_slug": "2023-2024",
      "format": "html",
      "text": "Present : Senator Nicole Mitchell - Vice Chair, Senator Bruce D. Anderson, Senator Calvin K. Bahr, Senator Jim Carlson, Senator Steve A. Cwodzinski, Senator Steve Drazkowski, Senator Omar Fateh, Senator Heather Gustafson, Senator John R. Jasinski, Senator Mark W. Koran, Senator Andrew R. Lang, Senator Erin K. Maye Quade, Senator Kelly L. Morrison, Senator Erin P. Murphy\n Absent : No Members Absent\n Senator Erin P. Murphy called the meeting to order at 10:08 am.\n Call to order \n Senator Mitchell assumed the gavel. \n S.F. 1426: Senator Murphy: Types of collateral the Executive Council may approve for deposit \nspecification with the commissioner of management and budget. \n Chair Mitchell took SF1426 off the table; testimony was heard from David Kelliher Minnesota Historical Society and Stacie Christensen Deputy Commissioner, Department of Administration \n Senator Murphy moved SF1426A10. \n Roll call requested. \n Chair Mitchell - YES\n Lead Anderson - NO\n Senator Bahr - NO\n Senator Carlson - YES\n Senator Cwodzinski - YES\n Senator Drazkowski - NO\n Senator Fateh - YES\n Senator Gustafson - YES\n Senator Jasinski - NO\n Senator Koran - NO\n Senator Maye Quade - YES\n Senator Morrison - YES\n Senator Murphy - YES\n With 8 voting YES and 5 voting NO, m otion prevailed. \n Senator Murphy moved SF1426A28.\n Roll call requested. \n Chair Mitchell - YES\n Lead Anderson - NO\n Senator Bahr - NO\n Senator Carlson - YES \n Senator Cwodzinski - YES \n Senator Drazkowski - NO \n Senator Fateh - YES \n Senator Gustafson - YES \n Senator Jasinski - NO \n Senator Koran - NO \n Senator Maye Quade - YES \n Senator Morrison - YES \n Senator Murphy - YES \n With 8 voting YES and 5 voting NO, m otion prevailed. \n Senator Koran moved SF1426A21. \n Roll call requested \n Chair Mitchell - NO\n Lead Anderson - YES\n Senator Bahr - YES\n Senator Carlson - NO\n Senator Cwodzinski - NO\n Senator Drazkowski - YES\n Senator Fateh - NO\n Senator Gustafson - NO\n Senator Jasinski - YES\n Senator Koran - YES\n Senator Lang - YES\n Senator Maye Quade - NO\n Senator Morrison - NO\n Senator Murphy - NO\n With 8 voting NO and 6 voting YES, motion failed.\n Stacie Christensen, Deputy Commissioner and General Counsel at Minnesota Department of Administration, joined Senator Murphy at the testifier table to answer member questions. \n Senator Murphy renewed her motion that SF1426, as amended, be recommended to pass and re-referred to Finance Committee. \n Roll call requested. \n Chair Mitchell - YES \n Lead Anderson - NO\n Senator Bahr - NO\n Senator Carlson - YES\n Senator Cwodzinski - YES\n Senator Drazkowski - NO\n Senator Fateh - YES\n Senator Gustafson - YES\n Senator Jasinski - NO\n Senator Koran - NO\n Senator Lang - NO\n Senator Maye Quade - YES\n Senator Morrison - YES\n Senator Murphy - YES\n With 8 voting YES and 6 voting NO, motion prevailed. \nSenator Murphy moved that S.F. 1426, be recommended to pass as amended and referred to Finance Committee. - MOTION PREVAILED .\n The meeting was adjourned at 10:59 am.\nSenator Erin P. Murphy\nAlexis Kise, Legislative Assistant"
    }
  ],
